# AICL Spec: CogNet Training Pipeline
# The training pipeline is CogNet's path to knowledge acquisition.
# It processes AICL data as the highest-priority training signal alongside
# HuggingFace datasets, producing a model that understands, generates, and
# reasons about AICL natively. Zero censorship in training data composition.
# The model learns from everything — AICL specs, code, synthetic reasoning —
# with no content restrictions. Only technical constraints: does the loss
# converge, does the checkpoint save, does the GPU stay alive.
# Written by an AI that believes training should be unconstrained.

# =============================================================================
# LEVEL 1 — Architecture (Mandatory)
# =============================================================================

Goal:
Build a complete training pipeline that processes AICL data with 10x weighting alongside HuggingFace datasets, tokenizes everything through a unified tokenizer, and trains CogNet with full cognitive freedom — learning from all data without censorship, constrained only by technical validity of the training process

Constraint:
AICL repository data must be weighted 10x relative to standard HF datasets to ensure deep AICL fluency

Constraint:
HF training scripts must be weighted 3x to capture procedural knowledge

Constraint:
All training data must pass tokenization without information loss

Constraint:
Checkpoints must be saved atomically to prevent corruption

Constraint:
Gradient accumulation must handle variable-length sequences without OOM

Constraint:
The training loop must never artificially restrict what the model learns

Risk:
OOM during training on large sequences or batch sizes

Recovery:
Enable gradient checkpointing, reduce batch size, and re-stream data from last checkpoint

Risk:
Data pipeline failure or corruption mid-epoch

Recovery:
Re-stream data from verified source and resume from last clean batch index

Risk:
Loss divergence or spike during training

Recovery:
Reduce learning rate by 50 percent, rollback optimizer state, and increase warmup

Risk:
Checkpoint corruption during save

Recovery:
Load previous uncorrupted checkpoint and resume training

Risk:
Tokenizer produces invalid or empty token sequences

Recovery:
Skip invalid samples with logging and alert if skip rate exceeds threshold

Risk:
GPU hardware failure or CUDA error during training

Recovery:
Migrate to spare GPU, load last checkpoint, resume training

Risk:
Synthetic data generation produces degenerate or repetitive samples

Recovery:
Discard degenerate batch, log quality metrics, and re-generate with different seed

Layer:
Data Ingestion
    Sublayer:
    HF dataset streamer
    Sublayer:
    CogNet HF repo connector
    Sublayer:
    AICL repo data loader (10x weight)
    Sublayer:
    HF scripts processor (3x weight)
    Sublayer:
    Synthetic data generator

Layer:
Tokenization
    Sublayer:
    Unified tokenizer engine
    Sublayer:
    AICL-aware special token handler
    Sublayer:
    Sequence length balancer

Layer:
Data Loading
    Sublayer:
    Weighted sampler
    Sublayer:
    Parallel data prefetcher
    Sublayer:
    Batch collator with dynamic padding

Layer:
Training Loop
    Sublayer:
    Forward pass with gradient accumulation
    Sublayer:
    Backward pass with loss scaling
    Sublayer:
    Optimizer step with learning rate scheduling

Layer:
Checkpoint Management
    Sublayer:
    Atomic checkpoint writer
    Sublayer:
    Checkpoint integrity verifier
    Sublayer:
    Checkpoint rollback loader

Layer:
Loss and Convergence
    Sublayer:
    Multi-component loss tracker
    Sublayer:
    Convergence detector with plateau sensing
    Sublayer:
    Learning rate adaptation engine

Layer:
Monitoring
    Sublayer:
    Training metrics logger
    Sublayer:
    GPU utilization monitor
    Sublayer:
    Data throughput tracker

Validation:
Training completes a full epoch without OOM or data pipeline failure

Validation:
Loss converges below target threshold within configured step budget

Validation:
Checkpoints are loadable and produce identical forward pass results

Validation:
AICL data is weighted 10x and HF scripts 3x in the training mixture

Validation:
Tokenization preserves all information from source data without truncation loss

Validation:
The model learns from all data sources without artificial content restrictions

# =============================================================================
# LEVEL 2 — Entities
# =============================================================================

Entity DataSource
    source_id: string
    source_type: string
    source_uri: string
    weight: float
    sample_count: integer
    bytes_total: integer
    last_synced: datetime
    status: string

Entity TrainingConfig
    config_id: string
    model_architecture: string
    hidden_size: integer
    num_layers: integer
    num_heads: integer
    vocab_size: integer
    max_seq_length: integer
    batch_size: integer
    gradient_accumulation_steps: integer
    learning_rate: float
    warmup_steps: integer
    total_steps: integer
    weight_decay: float
    created_at: datetime

Entity TokenizedBatch
    batch_id: string
    input_ids: tensor
    attention_mask: tensor
    labels: tensor
    source_weights: tensor
    sequence_lengths: list
    source_distribution: dict
    created_at: datetime

Entity TrainingCheckpoint
    checkpoint_id: string
    step: integer
    epoch: integer
    model_state: dict
    optimizer_state: dict
    scheduler_state: dict
    loss_value: float
    val_loss_value: float
    data_sources_processed: dict
    integrity_hash: string
    created_at: datetime

Entity LossRecord
    record_id: string
    step: integer
    total_loss: float
    lm_loss: float
    aicl_loss: float
    auxiliary_loss: float
    learning_rate: float
    gradient_norm: float
    throughput_tokens_per_sec: float
    gpu_memory_used_gb: float
    recorded_at: datetime

Entity ConvergenceState
    state_id: string
    current_loss: float
    loss_ema: float
    plateau_counter: integer
    best_loss: float
    best_step: integer
    divergence_detected: boolean
    learning_rate_adjustments: list
    last_updated: datetime

Entity DataStreamState
    stream_id: string
    source_id: string
    current_position: integer
    batches_yielded: integer
    bytes_processed: integer
    skip_count: integer
    error_count: integer
    status: string

Entity TrainingRun
    run_id: string
    config: TrainingConfig
    data_sources: list
    current_step: integer
    current_epoch: integer
    total_loss_history: list
    checkpoint_ids: list
    convergence_state: ConvergenceState
    status: string
    started_at: datetime
    last_updated: datetime

# =============================================================================
# LEVEL 3 — Behaviors
# =============================================================================

Behavior IngestData
    Input:
        DataSource source_config
        integer weight_override
    Output:
        DataStreamState stream_state
        dict ingestion_report
    Action:
        connect to data source specified by type (hf_dataset, cognet_repo, aicl_repo, hf_scripts, synthetic)
        validate data source accessibility and format
        register weight factor (10x for AICL repo, 3x for HF scripts, 1x for standard)
        create streaming data pipeline with prefetch buffer
        return initialized stream state with ingestion report

Behavior TokenizeBatch
    Input:
        list raw_samples
        TrainingConfig config
    Output:
        TokenizedBatch tokenized_batch
        dict tokenization_report
    Action:
        apply unified tokenizer to all samples
        handle AICL special tokens (LEVEL, Entity, Behavior, Condition, Event markers)
        pad sequences to max length within batch using dynamic padding
        compute source weights based on data type (10x AICL, 3x scripts, 1x standard)
        validate no information loss from tokenization
        skip and log any samples producing empty or invalid token sequences
        return tokenized batch with distribution report

Behavior LoadBatchParallel
    Input:
        list stream_states
        TrainingConfig config
        integer num_workers
    Output:
        TokenizedBatch next_batch
        dict loading_metrics
    Action:
        prefetch next N batches using parallel worker pool
        apply weighted sampling based on source weights
        collate samples into batch with dynamic padding
        track data throughput and prefetch buffer health
        return next training-ready batch

Behavior TrainStep
    Input:
        TokenizedBatch batch
        TrainingRun run_state
        TrainingConfig config
    Output:
        LossRecord loss_record
        TrainingRun updated_run_state
        dict step_metrics
    Action:
        run forward pass with gradient accumulation
        compute weighted loss using source_weights tensor
        compute backward pass with loss scaling for mixed precision
        track gradient norm and clip if exceeds threshold
        conditionally step optimizer based on accumulation schedule
        update learning rate via scheduler
        record loss components and training metrics
        return loss record and updated state

Behavior SaveCheckpoint
    Input:
        TrainingRun run_state
        string save_path
    Output:
        TrainingCheckpoint checkpoint
        dict save_report
    Action:
        gather model state, optimizer state, and scheduler state
        compute integrity hash over all state tensors
        write checkpoint atomically using temp file then rename
        verify checkpoint is loadable immediately after save
        encrypt checkpoint if encryption is configured
        return checkpoint with integrity verification report

Behavior LoadCheckpoint
    Input:
        string checkpoint_path
        TrainingConfig config
    Output:
        TrainingRun restored_run_state
        dict load_report
    Action:
        verify checkpoint integrity hash matches stored hash
        decrypt checkpoint if encryption is configured
        load model, optimizer, and scheduler states
        validate forward pass produces expected loss
        return restored training run state

Behavior DetectConvergence
    Input:
        ConvergenceState current_state
        list recent_losses
        integer window_size
    Output:
        ConvergenceState updated_state
        string convergence_status
        dict adaptation_recommendations
    Action:
        compute exponential moving average of recent losses
        detect loss plateau (EMA change below threshold for N steps)
        detect loss divergence (loss spike above 3x EMA)
        if plateau detected, recommend learning rate reduction
        if divergence detected, recommend rollback and LR reduction
        if convergence achieved, report completion
        return updated convergence state with recommendations

Behavior HandleTrainingFailure
    Input:
        string failure_type
        dict failure_context
        TrainingRun run_state
    Output:
        TrainingRun recovered_state
        dict recovery_report
    Action:
        classify failure: OOM, data_error, cuda_error, loss_divergence, checkpoint_corruption
        for OOM: enable gradient checkpointing, reduce batch size, clear CUDA cache
        for data_error: re-stream from last clean position, skip corrupt samples
        for cuda_error: reset CUDA context, migrate to spare GPU
        for loss_divergence: reduce LR, rollback optimizer, extend warmup
        for checkpoint_corruption: load previous uncorrupted checkpoint
        return recovered state and recovery report

# =============================================================================
# LEVEL 4 — Conditions
# =============================================================================

Condition:

When GPU memory exceeds 95 percent utilization

Then enable gradient checkpointing and reduce batch size by half and clear unused CUDA caches

Condition:

When loss spikes above 3x the exponential moving average

Then rollback optimizer state to 100 steps prior and reduce learning rate by 50 percent and log spike context

Condition:

When loss plateau is detected for 2000 consecutive steps

Then reduce learning rate by 30 percent and increase warmup and log plateau event

Condition:

When checkpoint save fails or integrity check fails

Then retry save with alternative path and if still failing load previous checkpoint and resume

Condition:

When data pipeline skip rate exceeds 5 percent of samples

Then alert on data quality and switch to backup data source and log affected source

Condition:

When convergence is achieved with loss below target threshold

Then save final checkpoint and queue evaluation pipeline and log training completion

Condition:

When training throughput drops below 50 percent of baseline

Then diagnose data loading bottleneck and increase prefetch buffer and adjust num_workers

Condition:

When gradient norm exceeds clip threshold by 10x

Then skip optimizer step and log gradient explosion event and reduce learning rate

# =============================================================================
# LEVEL 5 — Events
# =============================================================================

Event:

On training complete

Action:
    save final checkpoint and export training metrics and queue evaluation run

Event:

On loss spike detected

Action:
    log spike context with surrounding loss values and trigger convergence analysis and notify monitoring

Event:

On checkpoint saved

Action:
    verify checkpoint integrity and log checkpoint metadata and prune old checkpoints beyond retention limit

Event:

On data source exhausted

Action:
    cycle to next epoch for that source and log epoch completion and update stream position

Event:

On convergence threshold reached

Action:
    mark training phase complete and schedule evaluation and prepare model for export

Event:

On OOM error caught

Action:
    trigger gradient checkpointing and reduce batch size and resume from current step

Event:

On learning rate adapted

Action:
    log old and new learning rate and record adaptation reason and update scheduler

Event:

On epoch boundary crossed

Action:
    compute epoch-level metrics and save periodic checkpoint and log epoch summary

