Priority:
Loss convergence speed over checkpoint frequency

# =============================================================================
# LEVEL 8 — Learning
# =============================================================================

Learn:

Optimal learning rate schedule for CogNet architecture

Goal:
    achieve fastest convergence without divergence

Adapt:

Learning rate based on loss plateau detection

Based on:
    loss EMA trend, plateau duration, and divergence history

Learn:

Optimal batch size for given GPU memory

Goal:
    maximize throughput while staying within memory limits

Adapt:

Batch size based on GPU memory utilization patterns

Based on:
    peak memory usage, gradient checkpointing overhead, and sequence length distribution

Learn:

Optimal data mixture weights across sources

Goal:
    maximize AICL fluency while maintaining general language quality

Adapt:

Source weights based on per-source loss trends

Based on:
    per-source loss curves, evaluation benchmarks, and AICL generation quality

Learn:

Optimal gradient accumulation steps

Goal:
    balance memory efficiency with training stability

Adapt:

Accumulation steps based on gradient variance

Based on:
    gradient norm variance, loss smoothness, and memory pressure signals

